  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Continuous Ensemble Weather Forecasting with Diffusion Models\n",
        "\n",
        "Educational notebook accompanying the scientific review of:\n",
        "\n",
        "> Andrae, Landelius, Oskarsson & Lindsten (2024). *Continuous Ensemble Weather Forecasting with Diffusion models*. [arXiv:2410.05431](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.05431)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning goals\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Motivate **probabilistic ensembles** for weather risk and renewable-energy decisions.\n",
        "2. Contrast **autoregressive** vs **lead-time–conditioned continuous** forecasting.\n",
        "3. Build a lightweight analogue of **Continuous Ensemble Forecasting** (fixed / OU noise).\n",
        "4. Combine both ideas in an **ARCI-style** hybrid (autoregressive anchors + continuous interpolation).\n",
        "5. Evaluate with **RMSE**, **CRPS**, and **Spread/Skill Ratio (SSR)**.\n",
        "\n",
        "> This notebook uses **synthetic** fields for reproducibility. It is **not** a full U-Net diffusion reimplementation of the paper. Swap in WeatherBench/ERA5 when ready."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1) Imports and configuration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from __future__ import annotations\n",
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.style.use(\"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\")\n",
        "RNG = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUTS = Path(\"../outputs\")\n",
        "ASSETS = Path(\"../assets\")\n",
        "OUTPUTS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "ASSETS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "N_LAT, N_LON = 16, 32\n",
        "N_ENS = 30\n",
        "TOTAL_HOURS = 240\n",
        "AR_STEP = 24\n",
        "INTERP = 6\n",
        "RHO = float(np.log(10.0))\n",
        "NOISE_SCALE = 2.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2) Synthetic weather proxy (t850-like field)\n",
        "\n",
        "We create a coarse lat–lon grid with a travelling wave and seasonal cycle. In a research workflow this would be replaced by ERA5 variables such as `z500`, `t850`, `t2m`, `u10`, `v10` from WeatherBench."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def lat_lon_grid(n_lat=N_LAT, n_lon=N_LON):\n",
        "    lat = np.linspace(-75, 75, n_lat)\n",
        "    lon = np.linspace(-180, 180, n_lon, endpoint=False)\n",
        "    lon_g, lat_g = np.meshgrid(lon, lat)\n",
        "    return lat_g, lon_g\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def true_field(t_hours, lat_g, lon_g, rng=None):\n",
        "    seasonal = 12.0 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * (t_hours % 8760) / 8760.0)\n",
        "    wave = 6.0 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * (lon_g / 360.0) - 2 * np.pi * t_hours / 120.0)\n",
        "    meridional = 8.0 * np.cos(np.deg2rad(lat_g))\n",
        "    field = 273.15 - 20.0 + seasonal + wave + meridional\n",
        "    if rng is not None:\n",
        "        field = field + rng.normal(0.0, 0.4, size=field.shape)\n",
        "    return field.astype(np.float64)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "lat_g, lon_g = lat_lon_grid()\n",
        "snap = true_field(0.0, lat_g, lon_g, RNG)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 3.5))\n",
        "im = ax.imshow(snap, cmap=\"magma\", origin=\"lower\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Synthetic t850-like initial state (K)\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"lon index\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"lat index\")\n",
        "fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, fraction=0.03)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3) Lead-time–conditioned mean (denoiser stand-in)\n",
        "\n",
        "In the paper, a neural score network \(S_\\theta(\\mathbf{z}; X(\\Omega), t, \\sigma)\) is conditioned on lead time \(t\).\n",
        "Here we use a transparent blend of persistence/tendency and climatology whose weight decays with lead time — illustrating why pure continuous forecasting weakens at long horizons."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def score_conditioned_mean(init0, init_m, lead_h, lat_g, lon_g):\n",
        "    tendency = init0 - init_m\n",
        "    persistence = init0 + tendency * (lead_h / 6.0) * 0.15\n",
        "    climate = true_field(lead_h, lat_g, lon_g, rng=None)\n",
        "    w = np.exp(-lead_h / 72.0)\n",
        "    return w * persistence + (1.0 - w) * climate\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "init0 = true_field(0.0, lat_g, lon_g, RNG)\n",
        "init_m = true_field(-6.0, lat_g, lon_g, RNG)\n",
        "\n",
        "leads_demo = [6, 24, 72, 168]\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(leads_demo), figsize=(12, 2.8))\n",
        "for ax, lead in zip(axes, leads_demo):\n",
        "    pred = score_conditioned_mean(init0, init_m, lead, lat_g, lon_g)\n",
        "    ax.imshow(pred, cmap=\"magma\", origin=\"lower\")\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f\"lead={lead}h\")\n",
        "    ax.set_xticks([]); ax.set_yticks([])\n",
        "fig.suptitle(\"Lead-time–conditioned mean forecasts\", y=1.05)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4) Continuous Ensemble Forecasting (Algorithms 1–2 analogue)\n",
        "\n",
        "Core idea from the paper: the probability-flow ODE solver is deterministic, so **shared / autocorrelated noise** across lead times yields a consistent trajectory that can be sampled **in parallel**.\n",
        "\n",
        "- `rho = 0` / fixed noise → Algorithm 1 style\n",
        "- `rho > 0` Ornstein–Uhlenbeck → Algorithm 2 style"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def ou_noise_process(n_times, shape, rho, rng):\n",
        "    z = np.zeros((n_times, *shape), dtype=np.float64)\n",
        "    z[0] = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=shape)\n",
        "    for i in range(1, n_times):\n",
        "        alpha = np.exp(-rho)\n",
        "        innov = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=shape)\n",
        "        z[i] = alpha * z[i - 1] + np.sqrt(max(1.0 - alpha**2, 0.0)) * innov\n",
        "    return z\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def continuous_ensemble_forecast(\n",
        "    init0, init_m, lead_hours, lat_g, lon_g, n_ens, rho, noise_scale, rng, fixed_noise=False\n",
        "):\n",
        "    n_leads = len(lead_hours)\n",
        "    shape = init0.shape\n",
        "    if fixed_noise or rho <= 0:\n",
        "        z0 = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(n_ens, *shape))\n",
        "        noise = np.repeat(z0[:, None, ...], n_leads, axis=1)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        noise = np.stack([ou_noise_process(n_leads, shape, rho, rng) for _ in range(n_ens)], axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "    out = np.zeros((n_ens, n_leads, *shape))\n",
        "    for j, lead in enumerate(lead_hours):\n",
        "        mean = score_conditioned_mean(init0, init_m, float(lead), lat_g, lon_g)\n",
        "        scale = noise_scale * (0.7 + 0.3 * (1.0 - np.exp(-float(lead) / 48.0)))\n",
        "        out[:, j] = mean[None, ...] + scale * noise[:, j]\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "short_leads = np.arange(1, 25, dtype=float)\n",
        "fixed = continuous_ensemble_forecast(\n",
        "    init0, init_m, short_leads, lat_g, lon_g, N_ENS, 0.0, NOISE_SCALE, RNG, True\n",
        ")\n",
        "ou = continuous_ensemble_forecast(\n",
        "    init0, init_m, short_leads, lat_g, lon_g, N_ENS, RHO, NOISE_SCALE, RNG, False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "i, j = N_LAT // 2, N_LON // 2\n",
        "truth_ts = np.array([true_field(h, lat_g, lon_g, None)[i, j] for h in short_leads])\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 4))\n",
        "ax.plot(short_leads, fixed[0, :, i, j], label=\"Fixed noise (Alg. 1)\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "ax.plot(short_leads, ou[0, :, i, j], label=\"OU noise (Alg. 2)\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "ax.plot(short_leads, truth_ts, label=\"Truth proxy\", linestyle=\"--\", color=\"black\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Lead time (h)\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"t850 proxy (K)\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Temporal continuity under different noise processes\")\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Mean |Δ| fixed:\", np.mean(np.abs(np.diff(fixed[0, :, i, j]))))\n",
        "print(\"Mean |Δ| OU:   \", np.mean(np.abs(np.diff(ou[0, :, i, j]))))\n",
        "print(\"Mean |Δ| truth:\", np.mean(np.abs(np.diff(truth_ts))))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5) ARCI: Autoregressive rollouts with continuous interpolation\n",
        "\n",
        "ARCI (Algorithm 3) iterates on a long step (e.g., 24 h) and fills intermediate hours with continuous sampling — retaining long-horizon skill while keeping fine temporal resolution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def arci_forecast(init0, init_m, total_hours, ar_step, interp, lat_g, lon_g, n_ens, rho, noise_scale, rng):\n",
        "    leads_block = np.arange(interp, ar_step + 1, interp, dtype=float)\n",
        "    n_blocks = int(np.ceil(total_hours / ar_step))\n",
        "    all_members, all_leads = [], []\n",
        "    cur0, cur_m, t0 = init0.copy(), init_m.copy(), 0.0\n",
        "    for _ in range(n_blocks):\n",
        "        block = continuous_ensemble_forecast(\n",
        "            cur0, cur_m, leads_block, lat_g, lon_g, n_ens, rho, noise_scale, rng, False\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        for jj, lead in enumerate(leads_block):\n",
        "            all_members.append(block[:, jj])\n",
        "            all_leads.append(t0 + float(lead))\n",
        "        cur_m = cur0\n",
        "        cur0 = block[:, -1].mean(axis=0)\n",
        "        t0 += ar_step\n",
        "    return np.stack(all_members, axis=1), np.asarray(all_leads)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "ens, leads = arci_forecast(\n",
        "    init0, init_m, TOTAL_HOURS, AR_STEP, INTERP, lat_g, lon_g, N_ENS, RHO, NOISE_SCALE, RNG\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"Ensemble shape (n_ens, n_times, n_lat, n_lon):\", ens.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Lead hours (first 12):\", leads[:12])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6) Probabilistic metrics (RMSE, CRPS, SSR)\n",
        "\n",
        "Following the paper's evaluation philosophy:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **RMSE** of the ensemble mean → deterministic skill of the mean forecast\n",
        "- **CRPS** → proper scoring of the predictive distribution (Gaussian closed form here)\n",
        "- **SSR** (spread / skill) → calibration; target ≈ 1 (diffusion models in the paper were often slightly underdispersed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def rmse(a, b):\n",
        "    return float(np.sqrt(np.mean((a - b) ** 2)))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def crps_gaussian(obs, mu, sigma):\n",
        "    sigma = np.maximum(sigma, 1e-6)\n",
        "    z = (obs - mu) / sigma\n",
        "    scores = sigma * (z * (2 * stats.norm.cdf(z) - 1) + 2 * stats.norm.pdf(z) - 1 / np.sqrt(np.pi))\n",
        "    return float(np.mean(scores))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def spread_skill_ratio(members, truth):\n",
        "    ens_mean = members.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "    spread = float(np.sqrt(np.mean(np.var(members, axis=0, ddof=1))))\n",
        "    skill = rmse(ens_mean, truth)\n",
        "    return float(spread / max(skill, 1e-8))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "rows = []\n",
        "for jj, lead in enumerate(leads):\n",
        "    truth = true_field(float(lead), lat_g, lon_g, RNG)\n",
        "    members = ens[:, jj]\n",
        "    mu = members.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "    sigma = members.std(axis=0, ddof=1)\n",
        "    rows.append({\n",
        "        \"lead_hours\": float(lead),\n",
        "        \"rmse\": rmse(mu, truth),\n",
        "        \"crps\": crps_gaussian(truth, mu, sigma),\n",
        "        \"ssr\": spread_skill_ratio(members, truth),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "metrics = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "metrics.to_csv(OUTPUTS / \"ensemble_metrics_notebook.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "metrics.describe()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7) Visualization dashboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "ens_ts = ens[:, :, i, j]\n",
        "truth_long = np.array([true_field(float(h), lat_g, lon_g, None)[i, j] for h in leads])\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(11, 8))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0, 0].plot(metrics[\"lead_hours\"], metrics[\"rmse\"], label=\"RMSE\", color=\"#1f4e79\")\n",
        "axes[0, 0].plot(metrics[\"lead_hours\"], metrics[\"crps\"], label=\"CRPS\", color=\"#c45c26\")\n",
        "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Skill vs lead time\")\n",
        "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel(\"Lead time (h)\"); axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"Score\")\n",
        "axes[0, 0].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0, 1].plot(metrics[\"lead_hours\"], metrics[\"ssr\"], color=\"#2a6f4e\")\n",
        "axes[0, 1].axhline(1.0, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\")\n",
        "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Spread/Skill Ratio\")\n",
        "axes[0, 1].set_xlabel(\"Lead time (h)\"); axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"SSR\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for m in range(min(8, N_ENS)):\n",
        "    axes[1, 0].plot(leads, ens_ts[m], color=\"#7aa2c4\", alpha=0.45, linewidth=1)\n",
        "axes[1, 0].plot(leads, ens_ts.mean(axis=0), color=\"#1f4e79\", linewidth=2, label=\"Ens. mean\")\n",
        "axes[1, 0].plot(leads, truth_long, color=\"#c45c26\", linewidth=2, label=\"Truth\")\n",
        "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Continuous ensemble trajectories\")\n",
        "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Lead time (h)\"); axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"K\")\n",
        "axes[1, 0].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "resid = ens[:, -1].mean(axis=0) - true_field(float(leads[-1]), lat_g, lon_g, None)\n",
        "vmax = max(float(np.max(np.abs(resid))), 1.0)\n",
        "im = axes[1, 1].imshow(resid, cmap=\"coolwarm\", vmin=-vmax, vmax=vmax, origin=\"lower\")\n",
        "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Final-lead ens. mean − truth\")\n",
        "fig.colorbar(im, ax=axes[1, 1], fraction=0.046)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.suptitle(\"Continuous Ensemble Weather Forecasting — Notebook Demo\", y=1.01)\n",
        "fig.tight_layout()\n",
        "fig.savefig(OUTPUTS / \"overview_notebook.png\", dpi=160, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "fig.savefig(ASSETS / \"overview.png\", dpi=160, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved:\", OUTPUTS / \"overview_notebook.png\", \"and\", ASSETS / \"overview.png\")\n",
        "print(metrics[[\"rmse\", \"crps\", \"ssr\"]].mean().to_string())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8) Takeaways and next steps\n",
        "\n",
        "| Paper concept | What this notebook showed |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Lead-time conditioning | Single model / mean map queried at any \(t\) |\n",
        "| Correlated noise | Fixed vs OU trajectories and temporal \(\\Delta\) |\n",
        "| ARCI hybrid | 24 h anchors + 6 h continuous fills |\n",
        "| Probabilistic verification | RMSE, CRPS, SSR dashboard |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Next steps for research replication**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Load WeatherBench ERA5 (5.625°) and standardize variables as in the paper.\n",
        "2. Replace `score_conditioned_mean` with a trained conditional diffusion U-Net / score network.\n",
        "3. Solve the probability-flow ODE (Karras et al., 2022) instead of additive Gaussian noise.\n",
        "4. Compare CI-only vs AR-only vs ARCI at 1 h / 6 h / 24 h resolutions.\n",
        "5. Report geographic skill maps and underdispersion corrections.\n",
        "\n",
        "Official paper code (authors): https://github.com/martinandrae/Continuous-Ensemble-Forecasting"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
